<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ottoman Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ottomans, Ottoman</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ottoman Empire was a Turkish Muslim state founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osman-i">Osman I</a> around 1300 in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, which grew to rule south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-east">Middle East</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. It conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> in 1453, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>, and absorbed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a> in 1517. A major rival of the Safavid, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> and Russian empires, it declined in the nineteenth century and was dissolved after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire.jpg" alt="Ottoman Empire" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Orwellianist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Ottoman_Empire_(1844%E2%80%931922).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
